ript output reveals something interesting - only three rows are flagged as header rows (has_th=True). However, when examining the page text, I notice the first row contains multiple th elements with complex rowspan and colspan attributes. \n\nThis discrepancy suggests the HTML parsing might not be capturing the full complexity of the header structure. The first row clearly contains header information, yet the parsing logic isn't recognizing it as such. I'll need to investigate why this specific row is being misidentified.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_561ea20b22d64188960c26cc","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport re\n\npage_text = open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1980_05_page_41.txt').read()\n\n# Let's look at the actual first few rows\nrows = re.findall(r'<tr>.*?</tr>', page_text, re.DOTALL)\n\nprint(\"First 3 rows:\")\nfor i, row in enumerate(rows[:3]):\n    print(f\"\\n=== Row {i} ===\")\n    print(row[:300])\n    print(f\"Has <th>: {'<th>' in row}\")\n    print(f\"Has <td>: {'<td>' in row}\")\n    tds = re.findall(r'<td>', row)\n    ths = re.findall(r'<th>', row)\n    print(f\"td count: {len(tds)}, th count: {len(ths)}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
